WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.284
The CIS Controls provide practical guidance and prioritization,

00:00:03.284 --> 00:00:07.265
but they do not remove the need for organizational judgment.

00:00:07.265 --> 00:00:10.847
Security programs must still consider business requirements, risk tolerance,

00:00:10.847 --> 00:00:13.634
regulatory obligations, resource constraints, and operational realities.

00:00:13.634 --> 00:00:18.410
The controls are a tool, not a complete security strategy by themselves.

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:22.789
They help teams focus, but teams still need ownership, governance, measurement,

00:00:22.789 --> 00:00:23.585
and improvement.

00:00:23.585 --> 00:00:24.779
Realistic expectations matter.

00:00:24.779 --> 00:00:27.565
The CIS Controls can strengthen security programs,

00:00:27.565 --> 00:00:32.740
but they should be used as part of a broader risk management approach.
